MOVIE GUESSING GAME

to play: run app.py with streamlit

Game explanation:
    You have five guesses to guess a movies title. You will get a row of emojis depicting the movie. For the first guess there will be one emoji shown, if you guess wrong a second one will apear if you guess wrong again the rest of the emojis will appear. 
    An LLM will evaluate your guesses and give you hints. After guessing wrong three times the LLM will let you know the genre of the movie, if you guess wrong again, it will tell you about an important character from the movie.
    After guessing the movie title wrong five times you have failed and a next round with a different movie will start. 
    You can see your game stats on the statspage. 
    The statspage depicts a bar chart showing you how often it took a certain amount of guesses to guess the movie right. It will also assign you one of three ranks according to your average amount of guesses per movie. Additionally you will see some statistics about the amount of movies guessed correctly and how many movies you failed to guess, as well as your average amount of guesses per guessed movie.


Problem we encountered and have not yet fixed:
    We read the emojis as a string, and get them seperately over the index. Some emojis consist of more than one part, leading to problems when displaying them. During the game, the case might occur that only one emoji is displayed for two or more guesses and with the next guess all the other emojis appear. 